  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116392",
      "title": "Rendering Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 269,
      "videoOrder": 257,
      "sourceHash": "6d05bf2832b3fdc0754fc8c1dd5c553ff76e606cce0b76d2cf0d377b8edc53b9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 1.86,
          "en": "So at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.86,
          "end": 6.84,
          "en": "I registered just one route here, this tasks route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.84,
          "end": 11.13,
          "en": "And that would ensure that if we visit our domain,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.13,
          "end": 16.13,
          "en": "so in my case here local host 4,200, during development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.81,
          "end": 22.233,
          "en": "/tasks, this component here would be loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 23.67,
          "end": 26.73,
          "en": "Now if you try doing that though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 26.73,
          "end": 28.773,
          "en": "you'll see that nothing changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 30,
          "end": 32.82,
          "en": "And the reason for that is that Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.82,
          "end": 37.82,
          "en": "doesn't know where to render this task's component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 38.07,
          "end": 41.13,
          "en": "Sure, we're telling it that this is the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 41.13,
          "end": 43.47,
          "en": "that should be loaded for this path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 43.47,
          "end": 46.29,
          "en": "but thankfully Angular does not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.29,
          "end": 50.91,
          "en": "automatically replace your entire UI with that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50.91,
          "end": 53.67,
          "en": "because that's typically not what you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.67,
          "end": 55.56,
          "en": "For example, we have a header here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.56,
          "end": 60.45,
          "en": "which we probably want to reuse across different routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 60.45,
          "end": 62.58,
          "en": "So replacing the entire screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.58,
          "end": 65.31,
          "en": "with the component we're defining here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.31,
          "end": 67.8,
          "en": "is typically not what we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.8,
          "end": 71.973,
          "en": "So Angular makes no assumptions regarding that, thankfully.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.93,
          "end": 75.63,
          "en": "And therefore you need to tell Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.63,
          "end": 77.793,
          "en": "where to render this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.81,
          "end": 81.84,
          "en": "And you do so by going to your app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.84,
          "end": 83.88,
          "en": "which is still the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.88,
          "end": 86.37,
          "en": "with which the entire application starts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.37,
          "end": 88.5,
          "en": "That's still the main component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.5,
          "end": 91.05,
          "en": "that gets rendered initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.05,
          "end": 93.06,
          "en": "And in that app component template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.06,
          "end": 97.35,
          "en": "you then need to place a marker for Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.35,
          "end": 99.96000000000001,
          "en": "so that it understands where it should render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.96000000000001,
          "end": 101.313,
          "en": "that route content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.33,
          "end": 105.63,
          "en": "And you do that with help of a special directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.63,
          "end": 108.33,
          "en": "which you can output in your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.33,
          "end": 110.85,
          "en": "And here I wanna replace this to-do paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.85,
          "end": 113.03999999999999,
          "en": "with that special directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.03999999999999,
          "end": 116.193,
          "en": "and that would be the router outlet directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.08,
          "end": 119.28,
          "en": "Now that's a directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.28,
          "end": 122.7,
          "en": "which by default is not understood by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.7,
          "end": 125.52,
          "en": "but you can of course teach it about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.52,
          "end": 128.46,
          "en": "By going to your component TypeScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.46,
          "end": 130.68,
          "en": "into the component decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.68,
          "end": 133.62,
          "en": "And by adding router outlet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.62,
          "end": 137.043,
          "en": "which must be imported to the imports array here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.88,
          "end": 140.37,
          "en": "That unlocks this directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.37,
          "end": 144.03,
          "en": "and that's then in the end, a placeholder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.03,
          "end": 146.52,
          "en": "or a marker to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.52,
          "end": 150.72,
          "en": "that tells Angular where the loaded component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.72,
          "end": 152.55,
          "en": "that's loaded because of routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.55,
          "end": 153.87,
          "en": "should be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.87,
          "end": 157.53,
          "en": "and it will be rendered next to this router outlet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.53,
          "end": 159.453,
          "en": "below it to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.04,
          "end": 164.94,
          "en": "Well, and with that, if you save that, things will change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.94,
          "end": 168.36,
          "en": "Now you can see this, there are no tasks yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.36,
          "end": 170.31,
          "en": "Start adding some text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.31,
          "end": 173.793,
          "en": "as I'm navigating to /tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.07999999999998,
          "end": 178.77,
          "en": "And if I go back to just local host 4,200,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.77,
          "end": 180.333,
          "en": "there's nothing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.2,
          "end": 185.85,
          "en": "If I go back to /tasks, this text reappears.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 185.85,
          "end": 186.72,
          "en": "And as you can see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.72,
          "end": 189.33,
          "en": "if you inspect this text here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.33,
          "end": 191.7,
          "en": "this app tasks component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191.7,
          "end": 195.333,
          "en": "this one here is rendered next to this router outlet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.52,
          "end": 200.07,
          "en": "And that is how routing works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.07,
          "end": 204.72,
          "en": "and how you ensure that routes are displayed on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204.72,
          "end": 206.19,
          "en": "But of course with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.19,
          "end": 209.16,
          "en": "we still don't really have a lot of routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.16,
          "end": 210.45,
          "en": "in this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.45,
          "end": 212.853,
          "en": "So that's what will change next.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
